summary:
  The silence scan after a landed episode is called on app, which has no
  such function, so a finished download throws before the queue moves and
  nothing else downloads until the widget restarts.

history:
  _podScanStart lives on the engine; the download handler asked app for it
  from 2026-08-09, when the pipeline followed the ledger into the engine.
  In QML that is a TypeError, raised on the line before the queue advance,
  so one finished episode stopped the line — and the landed file never got
  the silence map that skip-silence reads. The engine's own tests hid it:
  they hung a _podScanStart on the mock app, which is the one place the
  name ever existed. Found 2026-09-08, before the release that would have
  carried it into a fourth version.

target:
  package/contents/ui/PodcastEngine.qml

find:
              if (scanFile !== "") _podScanStart(scanFile);

replace:
              if (scanFile !== "") app._podScanStart(scanFile);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_podcastengine.qml::test_a_finished_download_lets_the_next_one_start
  and tests/qml/tst_podcastengine.qml::test_a_download_stages_url_then_curl_then_writes_the_ledger.
  Line-neutral.
